/-!
# Coefficient representatives with a common generic differential basis

Source: Illusie–Laszlo–Orgogozo, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé IV, §§2.1.4–2.1.12,
printed pages 50–53 (blueprint: lem-per-coefficient-field-generic-differential-basis).
The completion and Kähler differentials are Mathlib's canonical constructions.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace WeilConjectures

/-- (blueprint: lem-per-coefficient-field-generic-differential-basis)
The exact generic-basis conclusion for the specified coefficient section `s` and tuple `a`.
The algebra structure on `B` is induced by `s`. The scalar field `q.ResidueField` is canonically
Frac(B/q), via Mathlib's `IsFractionRing (B ⧸ q) q.ResidueField` instance. The vector indexed by
`i` is exactly `1 ⊗ d(a i)`, with the differential mapped into its maximal-ideal-adic completion.
Source: Illusie–Laszlo–Orgogozo, Exposé IV, §2.1.12, first paragraph. -/
def CoefficientSectionGenericDifferentialBasis
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] (e : ℕ)
    (s : IsLocalRing.ResidueField B →+* B) (a : Fin e → B) : Prop :=
  letI : Algebra (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) B := s.toAlgebra
  ∀ (q : Ideal B) [q.IsPrime], IsMinimalPrime q →
    ∃ b : Module.Basis (Fin e) q.ResidueField
        (TensorProduct B q.ResidueField
          (AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
            (KaehlerDifferential (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) B))),
      ∀ i : Fin e, b i = TensorProduct.tmul B (1 : q.ResidueField)
        (AdicCompletion.of (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B)
          (KaehlerDifferential (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) B)
          (KaehlerDifferential.D (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) B (a i)))

/-- (blueprint: lem-per-coefficient-field-generic-differential-basis)
A reduced complete Noetherian local ring in positive characteristic, all of whose minimal
components have the same positive finite dimension `e`, admits a coefficient section and `e`
elements of its maximal ideal whose completed exact differentials are a basis on every generic
component. `constants = none` means that no perfect subfield is specified. `constants = some ι`
specifies an inclusion of the perfect field `K₀`; the resulting section respects that inclusion.
Source: Illusie–Laszlo–Orgogozo, Exposé IV, §§2.1.4–2.1.12, printed pages 50–53.

Proof:
1. Choose a p-basis of the residue field, lift its elements, and use §2.1.4 to obtain an initial
   coefficient field. There are finitely many minimal primes; their quotients are complete local
   domains of dimension `e`.
2. By §§2.1.5–2.1.8, delete one finite set `J` of coefficient p-basis elements so that completed
   differentials over the remaining coefficient subfield `F` have generic rank `e + |J|` on every
   component. These modules are finite, generated by exact differentials, and compatible with
   passage to the generic fibres of the quotients.
3. In a domain, exact differentials of any nonzero ideal span the generic differential space:
   for a nonzero `u` in the ideal, the identity d(au) = a du + u da expresses every da in that span.
4. If `W` spans a vector space of dimension at least `r`, any `r` vectors can be made independent
   by adding vectors of `W` or zero. Induct on `r`, choosing the last correction outside the span
   of the preceding corrected vectors when necessary.
5. Induct over the minimal components. To adjust the lifts of the `J` p-basis elements on the
   next component without changing previous ones, use the intersection of the earlier minimal
   primes with the maximal ideal. Its image on the next component is nonzero: multiply an
   element of the maximal ideal outside that prime by one element of each earlier prime outside
   it. Steps 3–4 choose corrections in this ideal, preserving residues and earlier independence.
6. Keep the old lifts outside `J` and the corrected lifts on `J`. Apply §2.1.4 again to obtain
   the new coefficient section, rather than using the erroneous subfield formula in §2.1.11.
7. A derivation kills pth powers. Finite p-monomial expansions show that derivations over the
   new coefficient field are exactly F-derivations killing the corrected `J` lifts: outside `J`
   the lifts coincide. The Leibniz rule, including its inverse formula, proves this equivalence.
8. The universal property of completed differentials identifies the new completed module with
   the quotient of the F-completed module by the differentials of the corrected `J` lifts.
   These finite modules are complete. On each generic component those `|J|` vectors are
   independent, so the quotient has dimension `e`.
9. Repeat the component induction of step 5 with `e` elements initially zero. Steps 3–4 make
   their exact differentials independent on each successive component while preserving all
   earlier ones. Generic dimension `e` makes them a basis on every component.
10. As in §2.1.12, multiply by a pth power of an element in the maximal ideal outside every
    minimal prime. Such an element is obtained by summing products supported on individual
    components. Its differential vanishes and its image in every generic field is nonzero,
    so the resulting tuple belongs to the maximal ideal and retains every basis property.
11. For specified perfect constants and `c` in that field, take compatible p-power roots `c_m`.
    The difference between their inclusion and the section of their residue lies in the maximal
    ideal. Raising to p^m shows that the difference for `c` lies in every arbitrarily high power
    of that ideal. Adic separatedness forces it to vanish, proving the constants compatibility.
-/
theorem coefficient_field_generic_differential_basis
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime]
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [IsReduced B]
    [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) B] [CharP B p]
    (e : ℕ) (he : 1 ≤ e)
    (hequidim : ∀ q : Ideal B, IsMinimalPrime q →
      ringKrullDim (B ⧸ q) = (e : WithBot ℕ∞))
    (K₀ : Type v) [Field K₀] (constants : Option (K₀ →+* B))
    (hperfect : ∀ ι : K₀ →+* B, constants = some ι →
      Function.Bijective (fun x : K₀ ↦ x ^ p)) :
    ∃ (s : IsLocalRing.ResidueField B →+* B) (a : Fin e → B),
      (IsLocalRing.residue B).comp s = RingHom.id (IsLocalRing.ResidueField B) ∧
      (∀ i : Fin e, a i ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal B) ∧
      CoefficientSectionGenericDifferentialBasis B e s a ∧
      (∀ ι : K₀ →+* B, constants = some ι →
        ∀ x : K₀, s (IsLocalRing.residue B (ι x)) = ι x) := by
  sorry

end WeilConjectures
